<section class="lk-section lk-grounding" aria-labelledby="grounding-title">
  <div class="lk-wrap lk-grounding__grid">
    <div class="lk-grounding__copy">
      <p class="lk-kicker lk-kicker--green"><span></span> Keep claims supported</p>
      <h2 id="grounding-title">Change the writing, not the facts.</h2>
      <p>
        Rewriting often becomes more confident with every pass. VitaeContext tells agents to preserve supported
        claims, keep goals separate from verified experience, and flag evidence gaps before strengthening copy.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Use supported claims</strong><small>Base work on supplied context and sources.</small></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Keep evidence boundaries</strong><small>Do not turn intent or inference into experience.</small></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Adapt for the surface</strong><small>Change structure and language, not facts.</small></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="lk-grounding__visual" aria-label="Comparison between fact drift and grounded adaptation">
      <div class="lk-grounding__source">
        <small>SUPPORTED SOURCE</small>
        <p>Built and maintains an open-source toolkit of portable agent skills.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lk-grounding__paths">
        <div class="lk-drift-path">
          <span>Repeated rewrite</span>
          <p>“Created a revolutionary career growth platform.”</p>
          <strong>Evidence disappeared</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="lk-grounded-path">
          <span>Context + skill</span>
          <p>“Maintains an open-source toolkit of portable agent skills.”</p>
          <strong><i>✓</i> Claim stays supported</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
